  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0.0,
      "text": "Do you have cute eyes or hot eyes?"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 2.1,
      "text": "Here is how to tell!"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 2.9,
      "text": "Cute eyes are the ones your brain reads as young."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 5.7,
      "text": "They sit rounder and more open, with more of the upper lid showing."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 8.1,
      "text": "The outer corner stays level or dips down a touch, often with a little more white under the iris."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 12.9,
      "text": "Big and soft like a baby has, the shape your brain is wired to read as gentle and approachable."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 17.5,
      "text": "Think of the friend everyone calls cute, but nobody can quite explain."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 21.0,
      "text": "Chances are her eyes look exactly like this."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 23.0,
      "text": "Hot eyes are the opposite signal."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 24.8,
      "text": "They sit narrower and more horizontal, with less upper lid showing,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 28.0,
      "text": "and the outer corner lifts up instead of dropping."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 30.1,
      "text": "The eye looks aimed at you instead of open to you."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 33.1,
      "text": "Where cute eyes feel warm, hot eyes feel focused,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 36.2,
      "text": "and that pulls a face from approachable to the kind you cannot look away from."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 39.8,
      "text": "Think of the friend whose photos always look intense and serious, like a model, without trying."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 44.0,
      "text": "Whether cute or hot, neither is particularly better, they're just different."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 47.0,
      "text": "So which one are you?"
    }
  ],
